WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.740 --> 00:00:03.659
Sam and Bucky appear to have hit a snag.

00:00:03.659 --> 00:00:07.210
Production on the upcoming Disney+ series
Falcon and the Winter Soldier, which was to

00:00:07.210 --> 00:00:11.589
shoot for two weeks on the island of Puerto
Rico, has been suspended after twin earthquakes

00:00:11.589 --> 00:00:12.750
rocked the area.

00:00:12.750 --> 00:00:15.329
It's not yet clear when shooting on the series
will resume.

00:00:15.329 --> 00:00:19.180
The cast and crew of the series were all set
to arrive this week, but those travel plans

00:00:19.180 --> 00:00:20.599
had to be scrapped.

00:00:20.599 --> 00:00:25.340
The U.S. territory experienced an earthquake
measuring 6.4 on the Richter scale last Tuesday,

00:00:25.340 --> 00:00:29.599
the largest to hit the island in a century;
it was followed by another, smaller quake

00:00:29.599 --> 00:00:32.590
with a magnitude of 5.9 on Saturday.

00:00:32.590 --> 00:00:36.580
The quakes killed at least one and knocked
out power across the island, which has since

00:00:36.580 --> 00:00:39.160
mostly been restored, according to NPR.

00:00:39.160 --> 00:00:42.960
Falcon and the Winter Soldier was to shoot
scenes on the Northern portion of the island,

00:00:42.960 --> 00:00:45.670
in and around the small coastal town of Arecibo.

00:00:45.670 --> 00:00:49.370
Although the quakes struck off Puerto Rico's
southern coast, the town certainly felt its

00:00:49.370 --> 00:00:54.210
effects enough so that the Arecibo Observatory,
one of the largest facilities of its kind

00:00:54.210 --> 00:00:57.110
on Earth, was closed down as a precautionary
measure.

00:00:57.110 --> 00:01:01.680
Fortunately, a survey by drones detected no
damage to the observatory, which is key to

00:01:01.680 --> 00:01:06.090
U.S. scientists' efforts to detect asteroids
which may be swinging close by our planet.

00:01:06.090 --> 00:01:10.329
Since our boring old world has no Avengers
to counter such threats, let's hope the observatory

00:01:10.329 --> 00:01:12.810
is back up and running with all due haste.

00:01:12.810 --> 00:01:16.689
The filming of Falcon and the Winter Soldier
has so far proceeded with the level of secrecy

00:01:16.689 --> 00:01:21.310
one would expect from a Marvel Studios production,
and as such, we're not sure why filming on

00:01:21.310 --> 00:01:24.240
a sun-baked tropical island would be necessary.

00:01:24.240 --> 00:01:28.770
That said, recent leaked set photos do happen
to show an ornate Asian-style garden adorned

00:01:28.770 --> 00:01:32.869
with the flag of Madripoor a fictional East
Asian island which has appeared often in the

00:01:32.869 --> 00:01:37.540
pages of Marvel comics, usually in stories
having to do with Wolverine or the Hand, the

00:01:37.540 --> 00:01:40.259
ninja cult which is always harassing Daredevil.

00:01:40.259 --> 00:01:44.549
It may very well be that Puerto Rico was chosen
as a filming location for scenes taking place

00:01:44.549 --> 00:01:49.130
in Madripoor, with its natural beauty and
miles upon miles of beaches.

00:01:49.130 --> 00:01:52.659
In any event, it looks like Falcon and the
Winter Soldier's production is going to have

00:01:52.659 --> 00:01:54.520
to find a substitute, and quickly.

00:01:54.520 --> 00:01:56.509
Sorry, folks the truth hurts!

00:01:56.509 --> 00:01:58.549
"...I hate you."

00:01:58.549 --> 00:02:02.459
Of course, location scouting and securing
all of the necessary documentation required

00:02:02.459 --> 00:02:05.850
to shoot on location can be a time-consuming
process.

00:02:05.850 --> 00:02:09.330
There are also sure to be plenty of other
variables at play when it comes to adjusting

00:02:09.330 --> 00:02:13.890
Falcon and the Winter Soldier's filming schedule
to make up for the lost Puerto Rican shoot;

00:02:13.890 --> 00:02:17.580
it's not known whether the production was
to move to a different location or back onto

00:02:17.580 --> 00:02:22.060
another studio lot after shooting in Arecibo
was completed, but in either case, there's

00:02:22.060 --> 00:02:23.890
sure to be some scrambling.

00:02:23.890 --> 00:02:27.630
Even assuming that filming is able to resume
relatively quickly, there remains the fact

00:02:27.630 --> 00:02:31.500
that there are all kinds of potential snags
to be hit in searching for another location

00:02:31.500 --> 00:02:33.180
to sub in for Puerto Rico.

00:02:33.180 --> 00:02:36.870
At this point, we give Falcon and the Winter
Soldier a 50/50 chance of sticking to its

00:02:36.870 --> 00:02:41.680
announced fall 2020 debut but fortunately,
should the series' premiere be delayed, there's

00:02:41.680 --> 00:02:44.350
another player waiting to come off the bench.

00:02:44.350 --> 00:02:47.440
That would be WandaVision, which has hit no
such snafus.

00:02:47.440 --> 00:02:51.430
In fact, production has apparently gone so
smoothly on the series that it's already been

00:02:51.430 --> 00:02:56.000
pushed up from its announced spring 2021 premiere,
and is now said to be on track to drop on

00:02:56.000 --> 00:03:01.400
Disney+ in late 2020 a fortunate turn of events,
and one that ensures that the streamer will

00:03:01.400 --> 00:03:05.690
debut at least one of its hotly anticipated
MCU-set series this year.

00:03:05.690 --> 00:03:09.280
So, rest easy, Sam and Bucky Vision and Scarlet
Witch have your backs.

00:03:09.280 --> 00:03:13.540
We'll be sure to keep you up to speed on any
news regarding the anticipated premiere dates

00:03:13.540 --> 00:03:17.350
for WandaVision and the adventures of everybody's
favorite best frenemies.

00:03:17.350 --> 00:03:20.130
"Can you move your seat up?"

00:03:20.130 --> 00:03:21.130
"No."

